<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:06:31Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Airport malaria in Germany remains infrequent</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:804add3025d923a2c653278c6f4f6414168c261f9eda0ccb2a5c4cf19fe4f5f1</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:05:52Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T18:23:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/airport-malaria-in-germany-remains-infrequent/a-79333920--b6e9f1b4961f.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/airport-malaria-in-germany-remains-infrequent/a-79333920?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">An outbreak of malaria at Frankfurt Airport this summer has raised alarm. Experts believe parasites probably arrived in a passenger's luggage. But with the onset of fall, the risks of contracting the disease are low.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Ever more Israelis moving to and investing in Cyprus</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b96632efcbb9ccc1667d02f4bf56299c950938d6b5637f761a291d54fe31d527</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:06:07Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T15:08:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/ever-more-israelis-moving-to-and-investing-in-cyprus/a-79330240--f9d83a8ed500.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/ever-more-israelis-moving-to-and-investing-in-cyprus/a-79330240?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Over the past three years, more and more Israelis have been purchasing property and investing in Cyprus, with many moving to the island permanently. How has this changed the Cypriot economy and how are locals responding?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Canada and EU: A look at the bloc's special relationships</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:cab85cdb0c5701290814075a545ccbd028538d979bcbee70f6ee5bcbdaef58ef</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:06:10Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T14:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/canada-and-eu-a-look-at-the-bloc-s-special-relationships/a-79328797--41616c65f5bb.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/canada-and-eu-a-look-at-the-bloc-s-special-relationships/a-79328797?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Though Canada may be some distance from Europe geographically, closer political ties are in the cards. With talk of an associate membership, DW takes a look at other arrangements the EU has with particular countries.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>High-profile raids spotlight India's food-safety struggles</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:85a6f0a495b17f6569f7796141adf8e9eb8b7a7828d7edf321eb67f0775837fb</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:06:31Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T11:26:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/high-profile-raids-spotlight-india-s-food-safety-struggles/a-79324342--7a2317b19494.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/high-profile-raids-spotlight-india-s-food-safety-struggles/a-79324342?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Recent raids at luxury hotels and a wider crackdown on food companies have renewed the debate about food-safety standards and enforcement in India.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Aztec manuscript returns to Mexico after two centuries, on loan</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:fd5716672b6621e622b08a26264b05d664fc616f625f4791b5380123310ff10b</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-18T03:07:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/aztec-manuscript-returns-to-mexico-after-two-centuries-on-loan/a-79316983--e03b036933bc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/aztec-manuscript-returns-to-mexico-after-two-centuries-on-loan/a-79316983?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">For years, Mexico has demanded the return of a treasured manuscript. Now the Aztec relic is back home from France — but on loan.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Russian birth tourism to Brazil increases</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a279f3746e0e03a53baafa690b27dcf8240655d79239963ab2c573a6b5909073</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T19:19:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/russian-birth-tourism-to-brazil-increases/a-79312304--01a0fcbb92e2.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/russian-birth-tourism-to-brazil-increases/a-79312304?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Since Russia's full-scale invasion of Ukraine and stricter regulations in Argentina, more and more Russians are choosing to travel to Brazil to give birth to children, who will obtain Brazilian nationality.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>A war-fatigued and anxious Russia picks a new parliament</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4ecce66e2ae4d6331f746c8912c28dbf05ebe400b5bc5b145aadec34853cb4f5</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T16:42:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/a-war-fatigued-and-anxious-russia-picks-a-new-parliament/a-79312440--1588122e0cc9.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/a-war-fatigued-and-anxious-russia-picks-a-new-parliament/a-79312440?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Fuel shortages, drone strikes and mobilization rumors are fueling anxiety and war fatigue in Russia. As support for peace talks grows among Russians, the Kremlin is watching closely ahead of parliamentary elections.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Smuggling suspected as more rare animals seen in India</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:6f7904d7edc46966f02cb02afc62656b7fe4676ea30e8012c66e1025d4eb0c5b</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T13:18:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/smuggling-suspected-as-more-rare-animals-seen-in-india/a-79309352--d0621e7dbde3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/smuggling-suspected-as-more-rare-animals-seen-in-india/a-79309352?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Orangutans, rare reptiles and other exotic animals are popping up in India, suggesting the country is becoming a major destination for trafficked wildlife.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Fact check: How disinformation fuels Houthi-Saudi conflict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:7c7146a1d7e12718e9993bd6c2b3e614ff34c198394f5d9b306479e0a538117c</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T12:51:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/fact-check-how-disinformation-fuels-houthi-saudi-conflict/a-79307257--b5d0251bde9e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/fact-check-how-disinformation-fuels-houthi-saudi-conflict/a-79307257?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">As fighting between the Houthis and Saudi Arabia escalates, old and repurposed videos have flooded social media, with many presented as fresh footage from the front lines.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Serbian President Vucic criticizes Kosovo war crimes verdict</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:2f6eaf3a4fd04cdbdef9d3bc8405c8636d360d14bb4a7511085d6f68309cbacd</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T11:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/serbia-s-president-vucic-criticizes-kosovo-war-crimes-verdict/a-79307654--c1957e85b089.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/serbian-president-vucic-criticizes-kosovo-war-crimes-verdict/a-79307654?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The conviction of four former Kosovo Liberation Army leaders has drawn sharply different reactions across the Balkans. Serbia has accused the court of failing to fully address crimes against Serbs.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>King Charles, Earl Spencer clash over Diana death once again</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:1bfb338427b66c6480869be4556e0b93aec98fa7302eab6773ecccad99a77ab1</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-17T11:06:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/king-charles-earl-spencer-clash-over-diana-death-once-again/a-79305876--fe22dce63256.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/king-charles-earl-spencer-clash-over-diana-death-once-again/a-79305876?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Buckingham Palace has rejected criticism of King Charles III in a new book by the brother of his late wife, Princess Diana. Earl Charles Spencer has been a fierce critic of his former brother-in-law for decades.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>UK: Village votes to 'secede' in asylum center plan protest</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:86e4f46ff7d0c36814d8ae5f1216f8ec5463619ff5c890bac9e7a7d9639a8459</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T17:41:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/uk-village-votes-to-secede-in-asylum-center-plan-protest/a-79295826--f45e2135fb80.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/uk-village-votes-to-secede-in-asylum-center-plan-protest/a-79295826?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Residents of Piddington, a tiny, remote village in Oxfordshire in England, have staged a "referendum" on leaving the UK. They are objecting to plans to open an asylum reception center at a disused military base nearby.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Can Canada and the EU deepen ties to counter Trump?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:4aa52900378a58302bdc1b15d4cf778c63fc28ff4d8fee09070a0aea56d35dbc</id><updated>2026-09-18T19:04:57Z</updated><published>2026-09-16T16:50:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/can-canada-and-the-eu-deepen-ties-to-counter-trump/a-79295388--7ecef7e34741.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/can-canada-and-the-eu-deepen-ties-to-counter-trump/a-79295388?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Canadian Prime Minister Mark Carney is known for standing up to US President Donald Trump. Now he wants to forge a "unique alliance" with Europe. But what could such a partnership look like?</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
